From f5f4364cc63f8d8745734d61383480f5050251ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:49:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10208/11362] Seven writers: a finished run declares
 verdict_class null, not partial

REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3 (landed 080baaadff): choose the class by whether
the RUN finished, not by whether the RESULT was positive. These seven
writers used partial to mean mixed evidence; the consumer reads partial
as may-retry, so each finished run was re-run toward the 3-fail limit
(exp6513's task retired that way; exp6687's 2,983s synthesis was logged
FAIL and re-queued).

Each writer now emits null on its completed path, and each validator
rejects a partial declaration on that path, so a re-run cannot recreate
the mis-declaration (the exp3946 lesson: fix the writer, not only the
artifact). Status and honest_verdict strings that asserted the class
(complete_partial*, complete_terminal_partial) follow the class; the
6506/6510/6513 strings never named partial and are unchanged.

The deleted test-suite-mutation marker (e82b8c57) was armed by this
session's own baseline pytest run and lists only this session's authored
edit to experiment_6526 - not test damage. Artifact corrections and test
updates follow in separate commits.

